    {
        "title": "Electro-Shock Blues",
        "artist": "Eels",
        "discovered": 2017,
        "image": "ElectroshockBlues_Eels.jpg",
        "comment": "i have really distinct memories of this one. my girlfriend at the time was in the psych ward, which was out in the middle of buttfuck nowhere.<br><br>i would take the train out to the facility to visit her after school most days, and i'd listen to this album on the train. on the way back too, sometimes. it would be dark when i left.<br><br>thinking back, i think this album portrays that sort of chronic inescapable mental unwellness some of us are just born with in a really heartbreaking, almost angry way. which maybe overlaps with themes in my life at that time.<br><br>sometimes i wonder how she's doing these days. we never spoke again after we broke up."
    },
